{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin. the film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake as sean parker.\n\nthe movie starts with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, who is dumped by his girlfriend erica albright (played by rooney mara). in an attempt to get back at her, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and eventually gets mark in trouble with the university.\n\nmark is then approached by the winklevoss twins (played by armie hammer), who are also students at harvard, and they ask him to help them create a social networking site called \"the harvard connect\". mark agrees to help them, but eventually steals their idea and creates his own social networking site called \"thefacebook\" with the help of his roommates eduardo saverin and dustin moskovitz.\n\nthefacebook becomes a huge success and eventually spreads to other colleges and universities. mark and his friends become millionaires, but the success also brings a lot of problems. eduardo saverin, who was initially a co-founder of thefacebook, gets pushed out of the company by mark and sean parker, who becomes the new president of thefacebook.\n\nthe movie also explores the theme of friendship and betrayal. mark's friendship with eduardo is put to the test as thefacebook becomes more successful and mark becomes more and more obsessed with the site. the movie also shows how mark's relationships with his girlfriend erica and his friends are affected by his success.\n\nthe movie ends with mark sitting alone in a conference room, waiting for a verdict in the lawsuit filed by the winklevoss twins against him. the movie ends on a somewhat somber note, with mark realizing that his success has come at a great cost.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-made film that explores the themes of ambition, friendship, and betrayal. the movie features great performances from the cast, particularly jesse eisenberg and andrew garfield. the movie also features a great script by aaron sorkin, which is full of witty dialogue and clever plot twists. the movie is a must-see for anyone who is interested in the story of facebook and the people behind it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11627468466758728}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.6927862816373818e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.03940728306770325}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.3828373084834311e-05}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.24996495246887207}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.05494526028633118}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.15762676298618317}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -7.152560215217818e-07}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -8.821526535029989e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.529963462118758e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04119579493999481}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.014323282055556774}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529859336093068}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00017793569713830948}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0664076879620552}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0001918857597047463}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.08089515566825867}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.13929234445095062}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0020568647887557745}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0043732644990086555}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.004943050444126129}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.06923703849315643}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -0.0009750110912136734}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0542